## Single Directory Components (SDC) Rules

### Component Structure

Every component MUST have these three files:

1. component-name.component.yml - Metadata and prop schema
2. component-name.twig - Template markup
3. component-name.css - Component-scoped styles

### Component Schema Format

Use this exact format for component.yml files:

$schema: https://git.drupalcode.org/project/drupal/-/raw/11.x/core/modules/sdc/src/metadata.schema.json
name: Component Name
status: stable
description: Brief description of component purpose.
props:
type: object
required: - prop_name
properties:
prop_name:
type: string
title: Prop Title
libraryOverrides:
css:
component:
component-name.css: {}

### Using Components in Templates

Include components in Twig templates like this:
{% include 'jfm_blog:component-name' with { prop_name: value } %}

## Design System (css/tokens.css)

### Color Tokens

All colors use HSL format for easy adjustment:
--color-neutral-50: hsl(0, 0%, 98%);
--color-neutral-900: hsl(0, 0%, 10%);
--color-accent-500: hsl(217, 91%, 60%);
--color-text: var(--color-neutral-900);
--color-background: var(--color-neutral-50);
--color-link: var(--color-accent-500);

### Spacing Scale (8px grid)

--space-xs: 0.5rem; (8px)
--space-sm: 1rem; (16px)
--space-md: 1.5rem; (24px)
--space-lg: 2rem; (32px)
--space-xl: 3rem; (48px)
--space-2xl: 4rem; (64px)

### Typography

--font-base: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
--font-size-base: 1rem;
--line-height-base: 1.6;

IMPORTANT: All component CSS must reference these tokens, not hard-code values.

## CSS Coding Standards

### Structure and Naming

Use BEM-style naming:
.component-name { }
.component-name\_\_element { }
.component-name--modifier { }

### Required Patterns

- Mobile-first: Base styles for mobile, media queries for larger screens
- Logical properties: Use padding-inline, margin-block (not left/right, top/bottom)
- Custom properties: Reference tokens from css/tokens.css
- No !important: Exception only for prefers-reduced-motion override
- Scoped styles: Component CSS only affects that component

### Responsive Breakpoints

Tablet and up: @media (min-width: 768px)
Desktop and up: @media (min-width: 1024px)

## Accessibility Requirements (Non-Negotiable)

### Semantic HTML First

Always use semantic HTML5 elements:
✅ header, nav, main, article, aside, footer
❌ div class="header", div class="nav"

### ARIA Landmarks Required

<header role="banner">
<nav role="navigation" aria-label="Main navigation">
<main role="main" id="main-content">
<footer role="contentinfo">

### Focus Management

Always provide visible focus indicators:
:focus-visible {
outline: 2px solid var(--color-accent-500);
outline-offset: 2px;
}

### Skip Link Required

Every page must have skip to main content link:
<a href="#main-content" class="skip-link">Skip to main content</a>

### Color Contrast Requirements

- Body text: 4.5:1 minimum
- Large text (18pt+): 3:1 minimum
- UI components: 3:1 minimum

### Images

- Always require alt text in component schema
- Use empty alt="" for decorative images only

### Reduced Motion Support

Always include this in component CSS:
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
_, _::before, \*::after {
animation-duration: 0.01ms !important;
transition-duration: 0.01ms !important;
}
}

## Drupal Coding Standards

### File Naming

- Templates: kebab-case.html.twig
- CSS/JS: kebab-case.css, kebab-case.js
- PHP: snake_case.theme, snake_case.module
- Components: kebab-case/kebab-case.component.yml

### Twig Best Practices

Always include file docblock:
{#
/\*\*

- @file
- Brief description of template purpose.
-
- Available variables:
- - variable_name: Description
    \*/
    #}

Use semantic HTML and conditional rendering:

<article class="article-card">
  {% if image %}
    <div class="article-card__image">
      {{ image }}
    </div>
  {% endif %}
  <h2>{{ title }}</h2>
</article>

### PHP Preprocessing

Use proper Drupal hooks with documentation:

/\*\*

- @file
- Theme functions for JFM Blog.
  \*/

/\*\*

- Implements hook_preprocess_HOOK().
  \*/
  function jfm_blog_preprocess_node(&$variables) {
  // Add helpful variables
  $node = $variables['node'];
  $variables['created_formatted'] = \Drupal::service('date.formatter')
    ->format($node->getCreatedTime(), 'custom', 'F j, Y');
  }

## JavaScript Standards

### Vanilla JavaScript Only

Use modern ES6+ features, no jQuery or libraries:

/\*\*

- @file
- Brief description of functionality.
  \*/

(function () {
'use strict';

function functionName() {
const elements = document.querySelectorAll('.selector');
elements.forEach(element => {
element.addEventListener('click', handleClick);
});
}

function handleClick(event) {
// Handle event
}

// Initialize on DOM ready
if (document.readyState === 'loading') {
document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', functionName);
} else {
functionName();
}

})();

### Progressive Enhancement

- Site must work without JavaScript
- JS enhances, doesn't enable core functionality
- Forms submit traditionally
- Navigation works without JS

## Component Development Workflow

### Step-by-Step Process

1. Create component directory with three files
2. Define schema first in component.yml
3. Build semantic HTML in .twig template
4. Style with tokens in .css file
5. Test with checklist below

### Testing Checklist

- Keyboard navigation works
- Focus indicators visible
- Works on mobile viewport
- Color contrast sufficient
- Screen reader friendly
- Works without JavaScript

## Available Components

### site-header

Props: site_name, site_logo, menu_items
Purpose: Main site header with logo and navigation

### site-footer

Props: copyright
Purpose: Simple copyright footer

### article-card

Props: image, title, url, summary, date
Purpose: Blog post teaser for listings

### article-full

Props: featured_image, title, date, author, tags, body
Purpose: Full blog post display

### hero-cta

Props: heading, subheading, primary_cta, secondary_cta
Purpose: Optional homepage hero section

## What NOT to Do

### Never Add These

❌ Bootstrap, Tailwind, or any CSS framework
❌ jQuery or JavaScript libraries
❌ Build process (Webpack, Gulp, npm scripts)
❌ Sass/Less preprocessing
❌ External dependencies of any kind

### Never Do These

❌ Use !important (except reduced-motion)
❌ Skip accessibility testing
❌ Hard-code colors/spacing (use tokens)
❌ Use non-semantic divs when semantic HTML exists
❌ Forget to document complex logic
❌ Create components without proper schema

## Documentation Standards

### Inline Comments

Explain WHY, not WHAT:
/\*

- Using container queries here because card layout
- needs to adapt to container width, not viewport
  \*/
  .component {
  container-type: inline-size;
  }

### Component Documentation

Every component.yml should have clear description of purpose and all props.

### README Updates

When adding components, update README.md with usage examples.

## Questions to Ask Before Creating

1. Is this a new component or extend existing?
   Check if similar component exists, consider reusability

2. What's the semantic HTML?
   What's the right element (article, section, aside)?
   Do we need ARIA attributes?

3. Mobile-first approach?
   Design for mobile, enhance for desktop
   Test on small viewport first

4. Is it accessible?
   Can you navigate with keyboard?
   Is color contrast sufficient?
   Will screen readers understand it?

5. Does it follow Drupal conventions?
   Naming matches Drupal patterns?
   Follows coding standards?

## File Generation Checklist

When creating any file, ensure:

- Proper file header comments
- Follows naming conventions
- Uses design tokens (not hard-coded values)
- Includes accessibility features
- Mobile-first responsive
- Inline documentation for complex logic
- No external dependencies
- Tested with keyboard navigation

## Key Reminders

1. Simplicity over cleverness - Readable code beats clever code
2. Semantic HTML first - Style with CSS, not divs with classes
3. Design tokens everywhere - No magic numbers in component CSS
4. Accessibility is not optional - WCAG 2.2 AA minimum
5. Mobile-first always - Design for smallest screen, enhance up
6. Document the why - Comments explain reasoning, not what code does
7. Test as you go - Don't build everything then test
8. Progressive enhancement - Works without JS, enhanced with JS

## Common Patterns

### Creating New Component

Step 1: Create directory components/new-component/
Step 2: Create new-component.component.yml with schema
Step 3: Create new-component.twig with semantic HTML
Step 4: Create new-component.css using design tokens
Step 5: Test accessibility and responsiveness

### Adding Component to Template

In your template file:
{% include 'jfm_blog:component-name' with {
  prop_one: value_one,
  prop_two: value_two
} %}

### Styling Component

In component CSS, always use tokens:
.component-name {
padding: var(--space-md);
color: var(--color-text);
font-size: var(--font-size-base);
}

